  "reach_m": 0,
  "payload_kg": 8,
  "speed_mps": 0.5,
  "battery_h": 3,
  "bom_usd": 1150,
  "bom_assumptions": "Quantity-1 2026 prices. Base: 2 hub motors + drivers, 4-cell Li-ion pack, 2D lidar (~$100), depth camera (~$150), Raspberry Pi 5 + AI accelerator (~$150). Lift-and-tip: ~1.1 m telescoping linear actuator rated ~20 kg plus a tilt actuator and steel frame. Seal + reline: drawstring-pull motor and a bag-ring cartridge like today's self-sealing cans (e.g. Townew). Rest: can body, lid motor, load cell, bumper switches, charging dock (~$160).",
  "cost_drivers": [
    [
      "Mobile base: hub motors, battery, lidar, depth camera, compute",
      520
    ],
    [
      "Lift-and-tip mechanism: 1.1 m column + tilt actuator",
      320
    ],
    [
      "Auto seal + reline module with bag cartridge",
      150
    ]
  ],
  "env_changes_required": [
    "Kitchen -> garage door: an automatic door opener or a robot/pet flap (~$250-400); TrashBot has no arm to open doors.",
    "Threshold ramp at the garage step (~$60, shared with LaundryBot).",
    "A lid-lifter bracket on the landfill cart that the robot triggers by pressing against it (~$15-40).",
    "Keep a 0.4 m lane clear along the garage shelving (LaundryBot's dock moved 20 cm in house.json-matched paths).",
    "Uses refill bag cartridges (~$0.20 per bag), which the self-sealing mechanism needs."
  ],
  "tasks_excluded": [
    "Rolling the big cart to the curb on trash day: a 30 m outdoor trip with a curb, weather and a 50 kg cart needs a different robot; the user still does it once a week.",
    "Starting on its own (when full or on a schedule): on-demand only; the full sensor sends a phone notification and the user taps the button.",
    "Steps higher than ~3 cm without a ramp, and stairs.",
    "Sorting recycling and compost: it only handles the landfill bag.",
    "Rain and long outdoor trips: in this house the carts are in the garage, so the trip stays indoors."
  ],
